    <comment>NEW PACKAGE (supersedes sr#1372081): Suggests python-tree-sitter &gt;= 0.22 instead of Requires, matching tree-sitter-bash, so ring1/product installcheck does not demand a non-ring package.

- Convert the Python binding to the shared %treesitter_python_install
  loader: the compiled _binding extension is not built, so the parser
  is not compiled a second time and no python devel/pip/wheel
  BuildRequires are needed.
- The python subpackage pins the grammar package exactly.
- Suggests python-tree-sitter &gt;= 0.22 instead of Requires,
  matching tree-sitter-bash, so ring1/product installcheck
  does not demand a non-ring package.
- Run a functional %check parsing PowerShell source through the
  shim; gated to suse_version &gt;= 1699 because python-tree-sitter
  does not exist in Leap 16.0.

INTERDEPENDENT REQUESTS - please stage together:
 * sr#1372054 - tree-sitter (python binding macros)
 * sibling new-grammar SRs from editors:tree-sitter
Needed for python-graphifyy.</comment>
